From da5cf504169d9090ba0a9c4200d303839a2d253e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikolajQ <mikolaj.q@wp.pl>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:31:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DefaultDeviceEffectsApplier: Apply minimizeRadioUsage and a
 location effect

ZenDeviceEffects can carry minimizeRadioUsage, but the default applier
ignores it, so modes have no way to take the device off the air for the
night. Turning location off is just as useful for a bedtime mode and
there is no effect for it at all.

Apply minimizeRadioUsage as airplane mode and add a "disable location"
extra effect that turns location off for the current user. Both only
undo what the mode did: if airplane mode was already on, or location
already off, when the mode started, they are left alone when it ends,
and a manual change while the mode is active is not reverted when the
effects are applied again. Whether the mode made the change is
persisted, so it is still undone after a reboot during the mode, also
when the mode ended while the device was off.

Toggling airplane mode during a call would drop it, so the change is
deferred until the call ends, like night mode waits for the screen to
turn off.

Both effects are hidden, so only the system (Settings) can set them.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I6b6514608bee3e98e1505805724c6644affde7c2
---
 .../notification/ZenDeviceEffects.java        |   7 +
 .../DefaultDeviceEffectsApplier.java          | 159 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../DefaultDeviceEffectsApplierTest.java      | 123 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 289 insertions(+)

